 possible on a whole  host of values and this will depend on  upbringing religion perspective point of  view temperament you name so I think  that more freedom in schools would be  good and a greater encouragement for  children to explore language rather than  having to parrot back rules or or  strategies that teachers try to  inculcate in them and I think that  because of the nature of language  teaching in schools people graduate  without any sense of their own  capability of exploring and discovering  and learning languages on their own so  we're hoping that our small effort and  the effort of other people who are are  putting things up on the web that all of  this will lead to more interest in  language learning it's very good for the  brain if you're going to do things for  your brain like Sudoku you may as well  do language learning you're going to end  up with with with more benefits in a way  you know we do share this goal that this  you know during this brief period that  we're on the earth we shared with a  whole bunch of other people in cultures  the more we can partake of these other  cultures the richer our lives will be I  believe not not everyone has to believe  that but at least those that are that  way inclined should realize that insofar  as language learning is concerned their  fate is very much in their own hands the  less complicated is it is the better you  become a better reader by reading not by  reading strategies you become a better  speaker of a language by doing a lot of  listening and reading an increasing your  vocabulary the less we hear from the  link  lists and other theorists the better off  we are I've posted in the past on this  subject have made reference to ruben  alvarez or brazil who promotes the idea  of creating hunger and that if you're  hungry enough your brain will come up  with the tools needed to achieve what  you what you want to achieve so that is  my little diatribe on Canada Day and  look forward to continuing and to do  this and I always appreciate any  comments from listeners thank you five
 

